{
  "sn8.5:0.1": "Linked Discourses 8.5 ",
  "sn8.5:0.2": "1. With Vaṅgīsa ",
  "sn8.5:0.3": "Well-Spoken Words ",
  "sn8.5:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn8.5:1.2": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "sn8.5:1.3": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "sn8.5:1.4": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "sn8.5:1.5": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "sn8.5:2.1": "“Mendicants, speech that has four factors is well spoken, not poorly spoken. It’s blameless and is not criticized by sensible people. ",
  "sn8.5:2.2": "What four? ",
  "sn8.5:2.3": "It’s when a mendicant speaks well, not poorly; their speech is principled, not unprincipled; they speak pleasantly, not unpleasantly; and they speak truthfully, not falsely. ",
  "sn8.5:2.4": "Speech with these four factors is well spoken, not poorly spoken. It’s blameless and is not criticized by sensible people.” ",
  "sn8.5:2.5": "That is what the Buddha said. ",
  "sn8.5:2.6": "Then the Holy One, the Teacher, went on to say: ",
  "sn8.5:3.1": "“Good people say well-spoken words are foremost; ",
  "sn8.5:3.2": "second, speech ought be principled, not unprincipled; ",
  "sn8.5:3.3": "third, speak pleasantly, not unpleasantly; ",
  "sn8.5:3.4": "and fourth, speak truthfully, not falsely.” ",
  "sn8.5:4.1": "Then Venerable Vaṅgīsa rose from his seat, arranged his robe over one shoulder, raised his cupped palms toward the Buddha, and said, ",
  "sn8.5:4.2": "“I feel inspired to speak, Blessed One! I feel inspired to speak, Holy One!” ",
  "sn8.5:4.3": "“T